{
  "title": "Order Field Provenance",
  "eyebrow": "example · checkout service",
  "lede": "How an <code>Order</code> row becomes the JSON the checkout page reads. Each column is a real record with its fields in declaration order; every arrow runs from the field it reads to the field it writes.",
  "caption": "<code>customer</code> fans out into <code>customerId</code> and <code>customerName</code>. Three amount fields converge on one <code>totalCents</code>. <code>internalNotes</code> and <code>createdBy</code> are dropped at the first hop. From the DTO onward the mapping is one-to-one; only the JSON names change.",
